.TH CHTTPCLI_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_declare_scoped \- declare a scoped chttpcli handle variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

chttpcli_declare_scoped(name)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro declares a chttpcli variable called name and uses the
cleanup attribute of GCC to destroy it automatically: when name goes
out of the scope, whatever path leaves the scope, the library destroys
the handle in the same way as chttpclient_destroy.

The macro sets the variable to CHTTPCLI_INVALID. To stop the cleanup
call, set the variable to CHTTPCLI_INVALID again before the exit of the
scope.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_construct_scoped (3),
.BR chttpcli_declare (3)
